WEBVTT

00:21.910 --> 00:24.920
- Today's goals
- Sell out at the cultural festival!!

00:21.910 --> 00:24.920
- Don't forget to separate the trash
- during prep work!!

01:04.280 --> 01:06.180
And now, a report on
the status of the typhoon.

01:06.740 --> 01:11.309
A powerful, Category 8 typhoon
has formed just off the southwest coast

01:11.310 --> 01:16.289
and is moving north-by-northeast
at 40 kilometers-per-hour.

01:16.290 --> 01:18.969
Barometric pressure in the eye is reported
to be around 970 hectopascals,

01:18.970 --> 01:21.829
with wind speeds in the surrounding
area reaching 40 meters-per-second.

01:21.830 --> 01:25.070
And peaking at 55 meters-per-second.

01:25.770 --> 01:30.120
Parts of Okinawa report up to
350mm of rainfall as of this morning,

01:30.730 --> 01:33.109
There is currently no precipitation
along the western side of Japan,

01:33.110 --> 01:35.819
but it has been suggested that
strong winds could bring thunder and rain,

01:35.820 --> 01:40.100
which may exceed 200 mm-per-hour in areas
experiencing particularly inclement weather.

01:40.700 --> 01:42.939
Don't grip it too
tightly or you'll crush it.

01:40.703 --> 01:45.120
Please take care in ensuring that you
are well-prepared for further developments

01:42.940 --> 01:43.940
Yeah, I know.

01:44.090 --> 01:45.119
Wow, you're quick!

01:45.120 --> 01:47.620
as roads and public transportation
are likely to be affected.

01:45.480 --> 01:47.620
Bet you're a quick eater too!

01:48.090 --> 01:49.459
Man, look at 'em.

01:49.460 --> 01:51.379
Hey, who are the ones fighting?

01:51.380 --> 01:53.759
Azuma-kun and Saijou-kun, looks like.

01:53.760 --> 01:55.509
Watch out. Ogino's here.

01:55.510 --> 01:57.096
What do you think
you're doing in there?!

01:57.120 --> 01:58.259
Where are the teachers?

01:58.260 --> 02:00.130
What do you mean,
"It doesn't matter"?!

02:01.220 --> 02:03.650
Who the hell cares about baseball anyway?

02:02.190 --> 02:03.649
Azuma, you shithead!

02:03.650 --> 02:05.179
That's enough, Saijou.

02:05.180 --> 02:06.629
Hey, what are you doing?!

02:06.630 --> 02:07.580
Let go of me!

02:07.581 --> 02:09.270
Hold still, damn it.

02:08.170 --> 02:09.510
Are you hurt, Azuma?

02:10.160 --> 02:11.160
Get back here!

02:13.090 --> 02:14.090
Ow...

02:18.990 --> 02:21.050
You boys really went at it, didn't you?

02:23.760 --> 02:24.910
Look straight for me.

02:27.530 --> 02:28.920
There, all done.

02:32.000 --> 02:34.089
Aren't you guys friends?

02:34.090 --> 02:35.930
What were you fighting for?

02:41.090 --> 02:44.799
Fine. I get it. You better explain
yourself after you cool off.

02:44.800 --> 02:45.710
You hear me, Azuma?

02:45.710 --> 02:46.710
'Scuse me.

02:52.140 --> 02:54.519
Maybe we just need to give them
time to work things out.

02:54.520 --> 02:59.530
This sort of thing could make
or break a lifelong friendship.

03:12.890 --> 03:13.890
Azuma.

03:15.610 --> 03:16.890
You really quitting?

03:20.300 --> 03:22.550
Yeah. My mind's made up.

03:23.200 --> 03:24.549
For real?

03:24.550 --> 03:27.140
You're gonna regret turning
your back on what you love!

03:29.110 --> 03:30.110
Azuma!

03:55.790 --> 03:58.739
The Category 8 typhoon continues
to increase in speed and intensity,

03:58.740 --> 04:03.300
making it the largest
typhoon we've ever seen.

03:59.800 --> 04:01.139
I guess we're under the storm now.

04:01.140 --> 04:02.489
What? I didn't know about this!

04:02.490 --> 04:04.050
I guess it finally reached land...

04:03.300 --> 04:04.770
Man, it's raining something fierce outside!

04:04.770 --> 04:05.979
Saijou, are you all right?

04:05.980 --> 04:07.519
I'm completely soaked.
What about the typhoon?

04:07.520 --> 04:09.189
We're under its umbrella now, apparently.

04:09.190 --> 04:09.980
What's gonna happen?

04:09.981 --> 04:11.080
Oh, welcome back.

04:13.090 --> 04:14.090
Hey!

04:14.380 --> 04:16.370
We've still got work to do.

04:16.880 --> 04:18.819
It's probably gonna get
canceled tomorrow anyway.

04:18.820 --> 04:21.069
Everyone else is staying to finish!

04:21.070 --> 04:22.819
Get off my back.

04:22.820 --> 04:23.869
Look...

04:23.870 --> 04:25.699
You guys gonna go at it again?

04:25.700 --> 04:28.309
Saijou, forget about him!

04:28.310 --> 04:29.310
You heard her.

04:30.420 --> 04:32.259
Azuma, you can't just run away like that!

04:32.260 --> 04:33.330
Leave me alone!

04:38.000 --> 04:40.330
Huh? What happened?

04:41.930 --> 04:42.760
It won't turn back on.

04:42.761 --> 04:45.589
I think I saw a flashlight
in here somewhere...

04:45.590 --> 04:46.520
Is everyone all right?

04:46.520 --> 04:47.200
Sensei!

04:47.200 --> 04:48.200
Sensei!

04:48.820 --> 04:51.450
Calm down, everyone. Listen up.

04:52.530 --> 04:55.410
The island received evacuation
orders a little while ago.

04:55.920 --> 04:58.269
But it's still too dangerous
to drive because of the winds.

04:58.270 --> 05:02.490
For your safety, the school decided
to keep you here until the storm passes.

05:03.190 --> 05:06.199
My mom will get worried
if I don't come home!

05:06.200 --> 05:07.590
Everyone, stay calm.

05:39.980 --> 05:41.480
Azuma!

05:50.990 --> 05:51.028
No Entry

06:10.170 --> 06:11.350
Stay away from me!

06:14.450 --> 06:15.930
I have to get help...

06:17.310 --> 06:18.710
Don't!

08:22.550 --> 08:23.930
S-Sorry.

08:25.630 --> 08:27.500
Are you hurt?

08:29.370 --> 08:31.570
Don't worry about me.

08:33.510 --> 08:35.910
Wait! Don't get up!

08:59.730 --> 09:00.849
So there they are.

09:00.850 --> 09:03.490
What's going to happen to us?

09:02.230 --> 09:03.489
It'll be over soon.

09:03.490 --> 09:04.850
I know, but still...

09:05.330 --> 09:06.679
It feels fine now.

09:06.680 --> 09:07.680
That's good to hear.

09:11.110 --> 09:14.110
Feels kinda exciting to get to walk
around school at night, doesn't it?

09:20.620 --> 09:22.539
Man, what's the matter with you?

09:22.540 --> 09:25.470
Hey, just shut up and
help carry these back.

09:26.120 --> 09:28.169
Here, I'll take it out for you.

09:28.170 --> 09:29.170
Thank you!

09:32.180 --> 09:33.180
Azuma?

10:12.980 --> 10:14.090
That voice...

10:14.830 --> 10:15.830
It's hot!

10:27.910 --> 10:29.000
Get up!

10:29.750 --> 10:32.480
I was too late.
The link is already complete.

10:40.820 --> 10:41.820
Here.

10:49.480 --> 10:50.500
Huh?

10:55.740 --> 10:56.740
Here.

11:17.920 --> 11:19.000
Is that yours?

11:23.030 --> 11:26.030
What were you doing on top of the tower?

11:27.920 --> 11:32.040
I was sent to this planet to rebuild it.

11:32.450 --> 11:33.450
What?

11:34.630 --> 11:36.769
That hole over there
is the eye of the earth..

11:36.770 --> 11:39.050
It goes all the way
down to the earth's core.

11:39.980 --> 11:42.050
I used that to dig the hole.

11:42.560 --> 11:43.749
You did?

11:43.750 --> 11:44.999
Yes.

11:45.000 --> 11:46.049
I did.

11:46.050 --> 11:51.650
When I am aligned with the eyes
of both the earth and the sky,

11:52.180 --> 11:54.060
this planet will be reborn.

11:55.120 --> 11:56.340
The eye of the sky?

11:56.940 --> 11:58.820
Reborn?

11:59.320 --> 12:02.070
I am controlled by this collar.

12:03.170 --> 12:07.090
When the sun rises,
I will be forced to become the conduit.

12:25.530 --> 12:27.100
There's nothing I can do now.

12:28.590 --> 12:32.099
You have to get away from here.
Go as far as you can.

12:32.100 --> 12:34.100
But then what about you?

12:34.720 --> 12:38.110
Thanks for the food. It was delicious.

12:50.210 --> 12:52.450
How long are we supposed
to stay here like this?

12:51.620 --> 12:51.660
- Please only take one box of rations.
- Please only take one box of rations.

12:56.140 --> 12:58.130
- Blankets here->
- Please only take one box of rations.

13:06.630 --> 13:08.599
Man, you're really good at pitching!

13:08.600 --> 13:09.909
You should join our team!

13:09.910 --> 13:11.169
Can I really?

13:11.170 --> 13:12.140
I'd love to!

13:12.141 --> 13:14.119
All right, sweet!

13:14.120 --> 13:16.120
We have practice tomorrow,
so you should come check it out!

13:14.700 --> 13:15.700
Saijou.

13:16.120 --> 13:17.150
Okay!

13:16.860 --> 13:18.020
Saijou!

13:17.150 --> 13:18.905
Please only take one box of rations.

13:18.020 --> 13:19.020
There.

13:18.021 --> 13:20.660
Blankets here->

13:21.050 --> 13:22.050
Saijou.

13:22.540 --> 13:23.649
Got a minute?

13:23.650 --> 13:25.099
What do you want?

13:25.100 --> 13:27.160
You were the one who
told me to leave you alone.

13:27.640 --> 13:29.429
I'm sorry about before.

13:29.430 --> 13:30.990
I have something important to tell you.

13:36.910 --> 13:39.170
You really expect me to believe that?

13:39.770 --> 13:40.839
It's true.

13:40.840 --> 13:42.659
Don't you think there's
something weird about this storm?

13:42.660 --> 13:44.049
If we don't do something
soon, she's going to...

13:44.050 --> 13:45.920
What makes you think this is "important"?!

13:46.230 --> 13:47.400
This is ridiculous.

13:48.930 --> 13:52.180
Saijou, something terrible's
going to happen if we don't stop it!

13:59.000 --> 14:00.890
Just quit it already.

14:01.500 --> 14:02.620
Saijou...

14:21.620 --> 14:22.949
Stop. It's no use.

14:22.950 --> 14:23.960
You have to run away.

14:31.100 --> 14:34.180
You're going to get hurt too
if you stay here with me.

14:34.670 --> 14:36.700
I want to do whatever I can to help!

15:12.530 --> 15:13.530
She's gone!

15:28.490 --> 15:30.030
What's happening to the sky?

15:31.110 --> 15:32.110
Don't do it!

15:35.980 --> 15:37.030
Azuma?!

15:47.650 --> 15:48.840
You can't be here!

15:49.600 --> 15:50.839
What are you saying?!

15:50.840 --> 15:52.109
We have to run away!

15:52.110 --> 15:52.650
No!

15:52.651 --> 15:53.840
You need to go, now!

16:04.590 --> 16:05.590
Azuma!

16:05.620 --> 16:06.880
Saijou!

16:05.980 --> 16:06.880
You okay?!

16:06.881 --> 16:08.109
Why are <i>you</i> here?

16:08.110 --> 16:09.610
What's that supposed to mean?

16:13.980 --> 16:15.870
Wh-What the hell is going on?

16:26.120 --> 16:27.340
That's the old gymnasium.

16:28.700 --> 16:29.800
Azuma, wait!

16:40.590 --> 16:41.590
Azuma, don't go!

16:56.390 --> 16:57.320
Let go of me!

16:56.390 --> 16:58.309
No! Don't go!

16:58.310 --> 16:59.779
It's way too dangerous!

16:59.780 --> 17:02.330
Let me go! I want to help her!

17:02.900 --> 17:05.329
Why are you trying to do everything alone?!

17:05.330 --> 17:08.830
You don't understand what this means to me!

17:11.890 --> 17:14.339
You're right, but I want to understand.

17:14.340 --> 17:15.840
I want to know how you feel.

17:18.110 --> 17:20.610
Azuma, I'm sorry about before.

17:22.000 --> 17:24.160
I thought you were just
trying to run from me.

17:26.970 --> 17:28.350
I think I <i>was</i> trying to run.

17:30.530 --> 17:36.570
I hated how I was always following
you places. It made me feel lame.

17:38.250 --> 17:40.020
But... I don't want to run anymore.

17:40.910 --> 17:42.470
I want to save that girl!

17:43.710 --> 17:46.500
Saijou, will you help me?

17:52.070 --> 17:54.510
We've always stuck together, haven't we?

18:03.490 --> 18:06.849
She told me that this typhoon
is the eye of the sky,

18:06.850 --> 18:09.489
and once she becomes the conduit,
aligned with them both...

18:09.490 --> 18:10.879
Once she's aligned?

18:10.880 --> 18:13.270
Something bad's going to happen, I know it!

18:15.640 --> 18:17.269
Wh-What the hell is this?

18:17.270 --> 18:18.280
I don't know.

18:18.920 --> 18:20.170
What do we do?

18:23.280 --> 18:25.410
She's being controlled by that collar.

18:26.360 --> 18:27.790
Azuma, don't do anything dumb!

18:39.300 --> 18:40.700
Just hang on.

18:46.340 --> 18:47.340
Let's go.

18:48.310 --> 18:49.520
One... two...

19:38.680 --> 19:40.610
Ow...

19:42.520 --> 19:43.710
Don't give up!

19:47.600 --> 19:48.870
Azuma...

20:53.980 --> 20:54.980
Hey!

21:37.270 --> 21:38.310
Here.

21:43.110 --> 21:44.110
Thanks.

21:44.860 --> 21:46.229
Man, this is sweet!

21:46.230 --> 21:47.080
What's it made of?

21:47.081 --> 21:48.539
Saijou, leave it alone.

21:48.540 --> 21:49.869
Why?

21:49.870 --> 21:51.199
You could get hurt.

21:51.200 --> 21:52.880
I don't want to hear that coming from you.

21:55.500 --> 21:56.620
Take care of yourselves.

22:03.590 --> 22:04.880
Well then...

22:05.880 --> 22:07.380
Wait, what's your name?

22:09.020 --> 22:10.020
Noruda.

22:13.280 --> 22:14.390
Noruda...

23:10.820 --> 23:13.660
Do you remember the road

23:14.120 --> 23:16.790
we walked along that day?

23:17.240 --> 23:20.410
The rough feel of asphalt under our feet

23:20.660 --> 23:23.290
and a gentle breeze tickling our faces.

23:23.920 --> 23:26.590
You said to me, "farewell",

23:27.090 --> 23:29.880
and I replied, "farewell", too.

23:30.170 --> 23:36.060
You didn't look back even
when you were far away.

23:50.860 --> 23:53.570
And the sun soared through the sky

23:54.070 --> 23:56.830
and headed for the opposing shore.

23:57.200 --> 24:00.120
It rolled along from there,

24:00.450 --> 24:03.210
finally slipping into the summer sea.

24:03.830 --> 24:06.500
"It feels so far away..."

24:06.840 --> 24:09.800
"Yet it feels so close..."

24:10.050 --> 24:18.050
I couldn't have described it better myself.

24:20.640 --> 24:26.309
When the rains came
pouring down without warning,

24:26.310 --> 24:33.199
our sodden hearts
clashed against each other,

24:33.200 --> 24:38.989
but despite it all, you'd
never looked happier.

24:38.990 --> 24:46.990
Once this rain lifts, I'll have
to ask you and find out why.

24:54.840 --> 25:01.269
I thought about the promise I'd
made with you, buried in my bag

25:01.270 --> 25:07.649
and rummaged around,
hoping to throw it your way

25:07.650 --> 25:14.029
But all my fingers
closed around was a towel

25:14.030 --> 25:18.660
and I ended up saying,
"Here. You can use this."

25:20.580 --> 25:24.250
What the hell am I doing?

25:27.830 --> 25:33.339
The pouring rain stopped without warning,

25:33.340 --> 25:40.389
and I waited until the
last raindrop had fallen.

25:40.390 --> 25:46.099
I should have told you in that moment,

25:46.100 --> 25:54.100
but I forgot again, and instead I
took your hand, saying, "Let's go."
